VBI({"OBJ-00400":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 32","d":"David's Contemplation on the blessedness of the one whose sin is forgiven (Psalm 32)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 32:1–11; Romans 4:6–8","v":"Blessed is the one whose transgression is forgiven and whose sin is covered: while David kept silent his bones wasted under the LORD's heavy hand, but when he confessed his sin the LORD forgave it; the LORD is his hiding place and promises to instruct and guide him, and mercy surrounds the one who trusts in Him"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 32","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"designation","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 32:1; Psalms 32","v":"A Contemplation"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 32; Romans 4:6–8","e":"PER-00661"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00401":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 33","d":"The psalm of praise to the LORD, by whose word the heavens were made (Psalm 33)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 33:1–22","v":"The righteous are called to praise the LORD with the harp, an instrument of ten strings and a new song; by His word the heavens were made, for He spoke and it was done; He gathers the sea as a heap, brings the counsel of the nations to nothing and sees all the sons of men; blessed is the nation whose God is the LORD, for no king is saved by an army, nor anyone by a horse"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 33:1","v":"Rejoice in the LORD, O you righteous"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00402":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 34","d":"David's psalm when he pretended madness before Abimelech, who drove him away (Psalm 34)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 34:7; Psalms 34:1–22","v":"David will bless the LORD at all times, for He heard this poor man and saved him out of all his troubles; the angel of the LORD encamps around those who fear Him; he bids all taste and see the LORD's goodness, and teaches the fear of the LORD: keep the tongue from evil and seek peace, for the LORD is near the brokenhearted and guards all the bones of the righteous"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 34","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 34","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"occasion","r":"Psalms 34","e":"EVT-01118"}],"nm":{"EVT-01118":"David feigns madness before Achish","PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00403":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 35","d":"David's plea that the LORD fight those who fight against him (Psalm 35)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 35:1–28","v":"David asks the LORD to plead his cause and fight those who fight him, letting the angel of the LORD chase them like chaff; false witnesses repay him evil for good, though he fasted in sackcloth when they were sick, and they hate him without a cause; he asks the LORD to awake to his vindication, and will praise Him in the great assembly"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 35","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 35","e":"PER-00661"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00404":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 36","d":"David's psalm of the wicked man's transgression and the LORD's lovingkindness (Psalm 36)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 36:6; Psalms 36:1–12","v":"The wicked man has no fear of God before his eyes, flatters himself and plots evil on his bed; but the LORD's mercy reaches the heavens and His faithfulness the clouds, His righteousness is like the great mountains (by the note, the mountains of God), and men trust under the shadow of His wings, for with Him is the fountain of life, and in His light they see light"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 36","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 36","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 36","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00405":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 37","d":"David's counsel not to fret because of evildoers (Psalm 37)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 37:1–40","v":"David counsels not to fret because of evildoers, who will soon wither like grass, but to trust in the LORD, delight in Him and commit one's way to Him; the meek shall inherit the earth and the LORD upholds the righteous; now old, David has never seen the righteous forsaken nor their children begging bread, while the wicked shall be cut off"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 37","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 37","e":"PER-00661"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00406":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 38","d":"David's psalm in time of chastening, to bring to remembrance (Psalm 38)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 38:1–22","v":"David begs the LORD not to rebuke him in wrath, for His arrows pierce him and there is no health in his bones because of his sin; his wounds fester, his friends stand aloof and his enemies lay snares, yet like a deaf and mute man he waits in hope, confesses his iniquity, and asks the LORD, his salvation, to hurry to help him"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 38","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 38","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 38","v":"To bring to remembrance"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00407":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 39","d":"David's psalm on the measure of his days, given to Jeduthun (Psalm 39)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 39:1–13","v":"David resolved to guard his tongue before the wicked, but as he mused the fire burned and he asked the LORD to show him the measure of his days, for every man at his best is but vapor and walks about like a shadow; his hope is in the LORD, and he asks to be heard, for he is a stranger and sojourner with Him, as all his fathers were"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 39","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 39","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 39","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 39","v":"Given to Jeduthun"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00408":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 40","d":"David's psalm of the new song, who came to do God's will (Psalm 40)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 40:1–17; Hebrews 10:5–7","v":"David waited patiently for the LORD, who drew him out of a horrible pit and miry clay, set his feet on a rock and gave him a new song; the LORD did not desire sacrifice and offering, but David came to do His will, with His law in his heart, words Hebrews applies to Christ; he proclaimed His righteousness in the great assembly, and asks Him to hurry to deliver him from evils more than the hairs of his head"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 40","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 40","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 40","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00409":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 41","d":"David's psalm of the one who considers the poor, betrayed by his familiar friend (Psalm 41)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 41:1–13; John 13:18","v":"Blessed is the one who considers the poor: the LORD will keep him alive and strengthen him on his sickbed; David's enemies wait for him to die, and even his familiar friend who ate his bread has lifted up his heel against him, words Jesus applied to His betrayer; the LORD upholds David in his integrity, and the psalm, and Book One, close with a blessing of the LORD God of Israel"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 41","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 41","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 41","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00410":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 42","d":"The sons of Korah's psalm of the soul that thirsts for the living God (Psalm 42)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 42:1–11","v":"Like a deer longing for streams of water, the psalmist's soul thirsts for the living God; tears are his food while men ask where his God is, and he remembers going with the festive multitude to the house of God; cast down, he remembers God from the land of the Jordan, the heights of Hermon and the Hill Mizar, and bids his soul hope in God"},{"p":"designation","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 42:1; Psalms 42","v":"A Contemplation of the sons of Korah"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 42","e":"GRP-00086"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 42","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"GRP-00086":"Korahites"}},"OBJ-00411":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 43","d":"The psalm that asks God to send His light and truth to bring the psalmist to His holy hill (Psalm 43)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 43:1–5","v":"The psalmist asks God to vindicate him against an ungodly nation and a deceitful man, and to send out His light and truth to bring him to His holy hill and tabernacle, where he will go to the altar of God, his exceeding joy, and praise Him on the harp; he bids his downcast soul hope in God"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 43:1","v":"Vindicate me, O God"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00412":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 44","d":"The sons of Korah's psalm of the deeds of old and of Israel cast off (Psalm 44)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 44:1–26; Romans 8:36","v":"The fathers told how God drove out the nations by His hand and planted Israel, who won the land not by their own sword but by His right arm; yet now He has cast them off, given them up like sheep for food, scattered them among the nations and made them a byword, though they have not forgotten His covenant; for His sake they are killed all day long, words Paul quotes, and they ask Him to awake and redeem them"},{"p":"designation","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 44:1; Psalms 44","v":"A Contemplation of the sons of Korah"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 44","e":"GRP-00086"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 44","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"GRP-00086":"Korahites"}},"OBJ-00413":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 45","d":"The sons of Korah's song of love for the King and His bride (Psalm 45)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 45:1–17; Hebrews 1:8–9","v":"The psalmist recites his composition for the King, fairer than the sons of men, who rides out in majesty for truth and righteousness; the King, addressed as God, has a throne that is forever and is anointed with the oil of gladness, words Hebrews applies to the Son; the queen stands at His right hand in gold from Ophir, the daughter of Tyre comes with a gift, and the royal bride and her companions are brought into the King's palace"},{"p":"designation","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 45:1; Psalms 45","v":"A Contemplation of the sons of Korah"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 45","v":"A Song of Love"},{"p":"feature","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 45:1; Psalms 45","v":"Set to 'The Lilies' (Hebrew Shoshannim)"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 45","e":"GRP-00086"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 45","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"GRP-00086":"Korahites"}},"OBJ-00414":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 46","d":"The sons of Korah's song of God their refuge, whose river makes glad the city of God (Psalm 46)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 46:1–11","v":"God is His people's refuge and strength, so they will not fear though the earth be removed and the mountains carried into the sea; a river makes glad the city of God, the holy dwelling of the Most High, and God is in her midst; the LORD of hosts, the God of Jacob, is with them, who makes wars cease to the end of the earth; they are bidden be still and know that He is God"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 46","v":"A Psalm of the sons of Korah"},{"p":"feature","r":"Psalms 46","v":"A song set for Alamoth"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 46","e":"GRP-00086"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 46","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"GRP-00086":"Korahites"}},"OBJ-00415":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 47","d":"The sons of Korah's psalm of the LORD Most High, King over all the earth (Psalm 47)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 47:1–9","v":"All peoples are called to clap their hands and shout to God, for the LORD Most High is awesome, a great King over all the earth, who subdues the nations under His people and chooses their inheritance; God has gone up with a shout, reigns over the nations and sits on His holy throne, and the princes of the peoples gather as the people of the God of Abraham"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 47","v":"A Psalm of the sons of Korah"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 47","e":"GRP-00086"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 47","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"GRP-00086":"Korahites"}},"OBJ-00416":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 48","d":"The sons of Korah's song of Mount Zion, the city of the great King (Psalm 48)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 48:1–14","v":"Great is the LORD in the city of our God, His holy mountain: Mount Zion, lofty and beautiful, the joy of the whole earth, the city of the great King, where God is known in her palaces as a refuge; kings who assembled against her saw it and fled in fear, as when the east wind breaks the ships of Tarshish; all are bidden walk about Zion, count her towers, mark her bulwarks and consider her palaces, to tell the next generation"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 48","v":"A Psalm of the sons of Korah"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 48","e":"GRP-00086"}],"nm":{"GRP-00086":"Korahites"}},"OBJ-00417":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 49","d":"The sons of Korah's psalm on the folly of trusting in riches (Psalm 49)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 49:15; Psalms 49:1–20","v":"The psalmist calls all peoples, low and high, to hear his riddle on the harp: those who trust in wealth cannot redeem a brother or give God a ransom to live forever; wise and foolish alike die and leave their wealth to others, and man in honor without understanding is like the beasts that perish; but God will redeem his soul from the power of the grave (or Sheol, by the NKJV note)"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 49","v":"A Psalm of the sons of Korah"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 49","e":"GRP-00086"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 49","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"GRP-00086":"Korahites"}},"OBJ-00418":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 50","d":"Asaph's psalm of God the Judge, who shines out of Zion (Psalm 50)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 50:1–23","v":"The Mighty One, God the LORD, calls the earth and shines out of Zion, the perfection of beauty, to judge His people; He does not need their bulls and goats, for every beast and the cattle on a thousand hills are His, but asks thanksgiving and vows paid to the Most High; He rebukes the wicked who recite His covenant yet join thieves and adulterers and slander their brothers"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 50","v":"A Psalm of Asaph"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 50","e":"PER-01496"}],"nm":{"PER-01496":"Asaph"}},"OBJ-00419":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 51","d":"David's prayer of repentance when Nathan the prophet came to him after Bathsheba (Psalm 51)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 51:1–19","v":"David asks God, by His lovingkindness, to blot out his transgressions and wash him from his sin, which is ever before him and was against God alone; brought forth in iniquity, he asks to be purged with hyssop and made whiter than snow, to be given a clean heart, not to be cast from God's presence nor have His Holy Spirit taken from him, and to be delivered from the guilt of bloodshed; God desires a broken and contrite heart, and David prays that He will build the walls of Jerusalem"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 51","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 51","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"occasion","r":"Psalms 51","e":"EVT-01278"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 51","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"EVT-01278":"Nathan rebukes David","PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00420":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 52","d":"David's Contemplation when Doeg the Edomite told Saul that David had gone to Ahimelech (Psalm 52)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 52:1–9","v":"David asks the mighty man why he boasts in evil, with a tongue like a sharp razor, loving lies more than truth; God will uproot him from the land of the living, and the righteous will say he trusted in his riches and not in God; but David is like a green olive tree in the house of God, trusting in His mercy forever"},{"p":"designation","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 52:1; Psalms 52","v":"A Contemplation of David"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 52","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"occasion","r":"Psalms 52","e":"EVT-01124"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 52","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"EVT-01124":"Doeg tells of David at Nob","PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00421":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 53","d":"David's Contemplation of the fool who says there is no God, set to 'Mahalath' (Psalm 53)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 14:1–7; 53:1–6","v":"The fool says in his heart there is no God; God looks down from heaven and finds none who does good; the workers of iniquity are put in great fear, for God has scattered the bones of him who encamps against His people; David longs for Israel's salvation to come out of Zion; the psalm nearly repeats Psalm 14"},{"p":"designation","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 53:1; Psalms 53","v":"A Contemplation of David"},{"p":"feature","r":"Psalms 53","v":"Set to 'Mahalath'"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 53","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 53","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00422":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 54","d":"David's Contemplation when the Ziphites told Saul he was hiding with them (Psalm 54)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 54:1–7","v":"David asks God to save him by His name, for strangers and oppressors seek his life without regard for God; God is his helper and will repay his enemies, and David will freely sacrifice and praise His name, for He has delivered him from all trouble"},{"p":"designation","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 54:1; Psalms 54","v":"A Contemplation of David"},{"p":"feature","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 54:1; Psalms 54","v":"With stringed instruments (Hebrew neginoth)"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 54","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"occasion","r":"1 Samuel 23:19; 26:1; Psalms 54","e":"EVT-01135","b":"inferred","c":"probable","w":"The title gives the Ziphites' words to Saul as 1 Samuel 23:19 gives them; they came to him again in 1 Samuel 26:1."},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 54","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"EVT-01135":"The Ziphites betray David","PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00423":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 55","d":"David's Contemplation on the treachery of a companion (Psalm 55)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 55:15; Psalms 55:1–23","v":"In terror David wishes for wings like a dove to fly away and be at rest, for violence and strife fill the city; it is not an enemy who reproaches him but his own companion, with whom he walked to the house of God, whose words were smoother than butter while war was in his heart; David calls on God evening, morning and noon, and bids all cast their burden on the LORD, who will sustain them"},{"p":"designation","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 55:1; Psalms 55","v":"A Contemplation of David"},{"p":"feature","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 55:1; Psalms 55","v":"With stringed instruments (Hebrew neginoth)"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 55","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 55","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00424":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 56","d":"David's Michtam when the Philistines seized him in Gath (Psalm 56)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 56:1–13","v":"Hounded all day by enemies who twist his words and lie in wait for his life, David trusts in God and will not fear what man can do to him; God counts his wanderings and keeps his tears in His bottle, and David will pay his vows, for God has delivered his soul from death"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 56","v":"A Michtam of David"},{"p":"feature","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 56:1; Psalms 56","v":"Set to 'The Silent Dove in Distant Lands' (Hebrew Jonath Elem Rechokim)"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 56","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"occasion","r":"1 Samuel 21:10–15; Psalms 56","e":"EVT-01118","b":"inferred","c":"probable","w":"The title has the Philistines seize David in Gath; 1 Samuel 21:10–15 tells how Achish's servants knew him there and he was very much afraid."},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 56","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"EVT-01118":"David feigns madness before Achish","PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00425":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 57","d":"David's Michtam when he fled from Saul into the cave (Psalm 57)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 57:1–11","v":"David takes refuge in the shadow of God's wings until calamities pass, crying to God Most High, who will send from heaven and save him; his soul is among lions whose teeth are spears, but his heart is steadfast, and he will awaken the dawn with lute and harp and praise God among the nations, whose mercy reaches the heavens"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 57","v":"A Michtam of David"},{"p":"feature","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 57:1; Psalms 57","v":"Set to 'Do Not Destroy' (Hebrew Al Tashcheth)"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 57","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"occasion","r":"1 Samuel 22:1; 24:3; Psalms 57","e":"EVT-01119","b":"inferred","c":"possible","w":"The title has David flee from Saul into the cave: he escaped to the cave of Adullam (1 Samuel 22:1), and later hid in a cave in the wilderness of En Gedi when Saul came in (1 Samuel 24:3)."},{"p":"occasion","r":"1 Samuel 22:1; 24:3; Psalms 57","e":"EVT-01138","b":"inferred","c":"possible","w":"The title has David flee from Saul into the cave: he escaped to the cave of Adullam (1 Samuel 22:1), and later hid in a cave in the wilderness of En Gedi when Saul came in (1 Samuel 24:3)."},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 57","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"EVT-01119":"David gathers four hundred men at the cave of Adullam","EVT-01138":"David spares Saul in the cave","PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00426":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 58","d":"David's Michtam on unjust judges, whom God will judge (Psalm 58)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 58:1–11","v":"David asks the rulers whether they judge uprightly, for they work wickedness and are like a deaf cobra that will not hear the charmer; he asks God to break their teeth and sweep them away, so that men will say there is a reward for the righteous and a God who judges in the earth"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 58","v":"A Michtam of David"},{"p":"feature","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 58:1; Psalms 58","v":"Set to 'Do Not Destroy' (Hebrew Al Tashcheth)"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 58","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 58","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00427":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 59","d":"David's Michtam when Saul sent men to watch his house to kill him (Psalm 59)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 59:1–17","v":"David asks the LORD God of hosts to deliver him from bloodthirsty men who lie in wait for him through no fault of his; at evening they come back, growl like dogs and prowl around the city, but the LORD laughs at them, and David sings of His power and mercy, for God is his defense and refuge in the day of trouble"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 59","v":"A Michtam of David"},{"p":"feature","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 59:1; Psalms 59","v":"Set to 'Do Not Destroy' (Hebrew Al Tashcheth)"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 59","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"occasion","r":"1 Samuel 19:11; Psalms 59","e":"EVT-01109"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 59","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"EVT-01109":"Michal lets David down through a window","PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00428":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 60","d":"David's Michtam, for teaching, from his wars with Syria of Zobah and the Valley of Salt (Psalm 60)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 60:1–12","v":"God has cast His people off and made the land tremble, yet He has given a banner to those who fear Him; He has spoken in His holiness that He will divide Shechem and measure out the Valley of Succoth, that Gilead, Manasseh, Ephraim and Judah are His, that Moab is His washpot, over Edom He casts His shoe, and over Philistia He triumphs; David asks who will bring him to the strong city of Edom, for through God they will do valiantly"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 60","v":"A Michtam of David"},{"p":"feature","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 60:1; Psalms 60","v":"Set to 'Lily of the Testimony' (Hebrew Shushan Eduth)"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 60","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"occasion","r":"Psalms 60","e":"EVT-01256"},{"p":"occasion","r":"Psalms 60","e":"EVT-01261"},{"p":"occasion","r":"2 Samuel 10:16–18; 1 Chronicles 19:6; Psalms 60","e":"EVT-01268","b":"inferred","c":"possible","w":"The title has David fight Mesopotamia; the Syrians he fought at Helam came from beyond the River (2 Samuel 10:16–18), and the Ammonites had hired chariots from Mesopotamia (1 Chronicles 19:6)."},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 60","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 60","v":"For teaching"}],"nm":{"EVT-01256":"David defeats Hadadezer king of Zobah","EVT-01261":"Eighteen thousand are struck in the Valley of Salt","EVT-01268":"David defeats the Syrians at Helam","PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00429":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 61","d":"David's cry to be led to the rock that is higher than he (Psalm 61)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 61:1–8","v":"From the end of the earth David cries to God to lead him to the rock that is higher than he, for God has been his shelter and strong tower; he will abide in His tabernacle under the shelter of His wings, and asks God to prolong the king's life for many generations"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 61","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"feature","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 61:1; Psalms 61","v":"On a stringed instrument (Hebrew neginah)"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 61","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 61","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00430":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 62","d":"David's psalm of waiting silently for God alone, given to Jeduthun (Psalm 62)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 62:1–12; Romans 2:6","v":"David's soul waits silently for God alone, his rock, salvation and defense, while men plot to cast him down and bless with their mouths but curse inwardly; men high and low are lighter than vapor, riches are not to be trusted, power belongs to God and mercy to the LORD, who renders to each according to his work"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 62","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 62","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 62","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 62","v":"Given to Jeduthun"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00431":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 63","d":"David's psalm when he was in the wilderness of Judah (Psalm 63)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 63:1–11","v":"Early David seeks God, his soul thirsting for Him in a dry and thirsty land; he has looked for His power and glory in the sanctuary, and since His lovingkindness is better than life he will praise Him, remember Him in the night watches and rejoice in the shadow of His wings; those who seek his life will fall by the sword, but the king shall rejoice in God"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 63","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 63","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"occasion","r":"2 Samuel 15:23, 28; Psalms 63, 11","e":"EVT-01295","b":"inferred","c":"possible","w":"The title sets the psalm in the wilderness of Judah, and it speaks of the king (Psalm 63:11); fleeing from Absalom, David crossed the Brook Kidron toward the wilderness and waited in its plains (2 Samuel 15:23, 28)."}],"nm":{"EVT-01295":"David flees from Jerusalem","PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00432":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 64","d":"David's prayer to be hidden from the secret plots of the wicked (Psalm 64)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 64:1–10","v":"David asks God to hide him from the secret plots of the workers of iniquity, who sharpen their tongues like swords and shoot bitter words at the blameless; God will shoot at them with an arrow and make them stumble over their own tongues, so that all men fear and the righteous are glad in the LORD"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 64","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 64","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 64","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00433":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 65","d":"David's song of praise awaiting God in Zion for His goodness to the earth (Psalm 65)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 65:1–13","v":"Praise awaits God in Zion, who hears prayer and provides atonement for transgressions; blessed is the one He chooses to dwell in His courts; He set the mountains in place, stills the seas and the tumult of the peoples, waters the earth from the river of God, provides grain, and crowns the year with His goodness, so that pastures and valleys shout for joy"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 65","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 65","v":"A Song"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 65","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 65","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00434":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 66","d":"The song calling all the earth to see the awesome works of God (Psalm 66)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 66:1–20","v":"All the earth is called to shout to God and see His awesome works: He turned the sea into dry land and they went through the river on foot; He tested His people like silver and brought them through fire and water to abundance; the psalmist will pay his vows in God's house with burnt offerings, for God heard his prayer and did not turn His mercy from him"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 66","v":"A Song. A Psalm"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 66","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00435":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 67","d":"The song asking God to bless His people, that all nations may praise Him (Psalm 67)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 67:1–7","v":"A prayer that God be merciful, bless His people and make His face shine on them, so that His way and salvation be known among all nations; the peoples are called to praise Him, for He judges them righteously, and the earth yields her increase as all its ends fear Him"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 67","v":"A Psalm. A Song"},{"p":"feature","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 67:1; Psalms 67","v":"On stringed instruments (Hebrew neginoth)"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 67","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00436":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 68","d":"David's song of God's march from Sinai and His procession into the sanctuary (Psalm 68)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 68:1–35; Ephesians 4:8","v":"Let God arise and scatter His enemies; the righteous sing to Him whose name is YAH, a father of the fatherless and defender of widows; when He marched before His people through the wilderness the earth shook and Sinai itself was moved; kings of armies fled, and when the Almighty scattered kings it was white as snow in Zalmon; the many-peaked mountain of Bashan envies the mountain God chose to dwell in; He ascended on high, led captivity captive and received gifts among men, words Paul applies to Christ; His procession enters the sanctuary with singers, players and maidens with timbrels, little Benjamin, and the princes of Judah, Zebulun and Naphtali; kings will bring presents for His temple at Jerusalem, envoys will come from Egypt, and Ethiopia will stretch out her hands to God"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 68","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 68","v":"A Song"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 68","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 68","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00437":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 69","d":"David's cry from the deep waters, hated without a cause (Psalm 69)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 69:1–36; Matthew 27:34; John 2:17; 15:25; Acts 1:16, 20; Romans 11:9–10","v":"David sinks in deep mire with the waters up to his neck; those who hate him without a cause are more than the hairs of his head; zeal for God's house has eaten him up, and he has become a stranger to his brothers and the song of drunkards; they gave him gall for food and vinegar to drink; he prays that their dwelling be desolate and that they be blotted out of the book of the living; God will save Zion and build the cities of Judah; the Gospels and Acts apply its words to Jesus and to Judas"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 69","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"feature","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 69:1; Psalms 69","v":"Set to 'The Lilies' (Hebrew Shoshannim)"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 69; Acts 1:16, 20; Romans 11:9–10","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 69","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00438":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 70","d":"David's plea for God to hurry to help him, to bring to remembrance (Psalm 70)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 40:13–17; 70:1–5","v":"David asks God to hurry to deliver him and to shame those who seek his life and mock him, and to let all who seek Him rejoice, for he is poor and needy; the psalm repeats the close of Psalm 40"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 70","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 70","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 70","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 70","v":"To bring to remembrance"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00439":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 71","d":"The prayer of one who trusted God from his youth, that He not forsake him in old age (Psalm 71)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 71:1–24","v":"The psalmist, who has trusted the LORD from his youth and was upheld by Him from birth, asks not to be cast off in old age when his strength fails, while his enemies say God has forsaken him; old and gray, he will declare God's strength to the next generation and praise Him with lute and harp as the Holy One of Israel"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 71:1","v":"In You, O LORD"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00440":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 72","d":"Solomon's psalm of the king's righteous reign from sea to sea (Psalm 72)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 72:1–20","v":"A prayer that God give the king His judgments and the king's son His righteousness, so that he judges the poor with justice and has dominion from sea to sea and from the River to the ends of the earth; the kings of Tarshish and the isles, of Sheba and Seba, will bring gifts, and the gold of Sheba will be given him; grain will wave like Lebanon on the mountaintops, his name will endure as long as the sun, and all nations will call him blessed; the psalm closes Book Two with a blessing of the LORD God of Israel and the note that David's prayers are ended"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 72","v":"A Psalm of Solomon"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 72","e":"PER-00765"}],"nm":{"PER-00765":"Solomon"}},"OBJ-00441":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 73","d":"Asaph's psalm of the prosperity of the wicked and the end he saw in the sanctuary (Psalm 73)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 73:26; Psalms 73:1–28","v":"Asaph confesses that he nearly slipped, envying the proud and wicked, who prosper at ease and ask how God can know, until he went into the sanctuary of God and understood their end, cast down in a moment; though his flesh and heart fail, God is the strength (by the NKJV note, the rock) of his heart and his portion forever, and it is good to draw near to Him"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 73","v":"A Psalm of Asaph"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 73","e":"PER-01496"}],"nm":{"PER-01496":"Asaph"}},"OBJ-00442":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 74","d":"Asaph's Contemplation on the sanctuary set on fire by the enemy (Psalm 74)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 74:14; Psalms 74:1–23","v":"Asaph asks why God has cast off the sheep of His pasture and bids Him remember Mount Zion, where He dwelt: enemies roared in His meeting place, broke down its carved work with axes and hammers, set His sanctuary on fire and burned all the meeting places of God in the land, and no prophet is left; yet God, King from of old, divided the sea, broke the heads of the sea monsters and of Leviathan (a sea creature of unknown identity, by the NKJV note), dried up mighty rivers and set the borders of the earth; Asaph asks Him to arise and plead His own cause"},{"p":"designation","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 74:1; Psalms 74","v":"A Contemplation of Asaph"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 74","e":"PER-01496"},{"p":"occasion","r":"2 Kings 25:9; Ezra 2:41; Psalms 74, 3–8","e":"EVT-01905","b":"inferred","c":"possible","w":"The psalm laments the sanctuary set on fire and the meeting places of God burned (Psalm 74:3–8), as the house of the LORD was burned when Jerusalem fell (2 Kings 25:9)."}],"nm":{"EVT-01905":"Nebuzaradan burns the temple and Jerusalem","PER-01496":"Asaph"}},"OBJ-00443":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 75","d":"Asaph's song of thanks to God the Judge, set to 'Do Not Destroy' (Psalm 75)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 75:1–10","v":"Thanks to God, whose name is near: at the time He chooses He will judge uprightly, and He holds up the pillars of the earth; exaltation comes from no quarter of the earth but from God the Judge, who puts down one and exalts another, and the wicked will drain the cup in the LORD's hand"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 75","v":"A Psalm of Asaph"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 75","v":"A Song"},{"p":"feature","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 75:1; Psalms 75","v":"Set to 'Do Not Destroy' (Hebrew Al Tashcheth)"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 75","e":"PER-01496"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 75","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"PER-01496":"Asaph"}},"OBJ-00444":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 76","d":"Asaph's song of God known in Judah, whose tabernacle is in Salem (Psalm 76)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 76:2; Psalms 76:1–12","v":"God is known in Judah; His tabernacle is in Salem (Jerusalem, by the NKJV note) and His dwelling in Zion, where He broke the arrows, the shield and the sword of battle; at His rebuke chariot and horse fell into a dead sleep; He arose to judgment to save the oppressed of the earth, and the kings of the earth must fear Him"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 76","v":"A Psalm of Asaph"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 76","v":"A Song"},{"p":"feature","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 76:1; Psalms 76","v":"On stringed instruments (Hebrew neginoth)"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 76","e":"PER-01496"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 76","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"PER-01496":"Asaph"}},"OBJ-00445":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 77","d":"Asaph's psalm remembering God's wonders of old at the sea, given to Jeduthun (Psalm 77)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 77:1–20","v":"In the day of trouble Asaph cried to God and refused to be comforted, asking whether the Lord would cast off forever and had forgotten to be gracious; then he remembered the years of the right hand of the Most High and His wonders of old: God redeemed the sons of Jacob and Joseph, the waters saw Him and trembled, His way was in the sea and His path in the great waters, and He led His people like a flock by the hand of Moses and Aaron"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 77","v":"A Psalm of Asaph"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 77","e":"PER-01496"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 77","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 77","v":"Given to Jeduthun"}],"nm":{"PER-01496":"Asaph"}},"OBJ-00446":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 78","d":"Asaph's Contemplation telling Israel's history from Egypt to the choosing of David (Psalm 78)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 78:1–72; Matthew 13:35","v":"Asaph opens his mouth in a parable, which Matthew applies to Jesus' parables, to tell the coming generation the LORD's works and law, that they may not be stubborn like their fathers: God did wonders in Egypt and the field of Zoan, divided the sea, led them with the cloud and the fire and split the rock; yet they tested Him in the wilderness, and though He rained manna and quail, His wrath struck down their strongest men; He sent the plagues on Egypt, led His people like a flock, brought them to His holy mountain and divided their inheritance; when they provoked Him with high places and carved images He forsook the tabernacle of Shiloh and gave His strength into captivity, then beat back His enemies, chose Judah and Mount Zion, built His sanctuary, and took David His servant from the sheepfolds to shepherd Israel"},{"p":"designation","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 78:1; Psalms 78","v":"A Contemplation of Asaph"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 78","e":"PER-01496"}],"nm":{"PER-01496":"Asaph"}},"OBJ-00447":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 79","d":"Asaph's lament that the nations have defiled the temple and laid Jerusalem in heaps (Psalm 79)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 79:1; Psalms 79:1–13","v":"The nations have come into God's inheritance, defiled His holy temple and laid Jerusalem in heaps (in ruins, by the NKJV note); the bodies of His servants are left for the birds and beasts with none to bury them; Asaph asks how long He will be angry, prays that He not remember former iniquities but help them, the sheep of His pasture, for His name's sake, and avenge His servants' blood"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 79","v":"A Psalm of Asaph"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 79","e":"PER-01496"},{"p":"occasion","r":"2 Kings 25:9; Ezra 2:41; Psalms 79, 1–3","e":"EVT-01905","b":"inferred","c":"possible","w":"The psalm laments the temple defiled and Jerusalem laid in heaps (Psalm 79:1–3), as the house of the LORD and the houses of Jerusalem were burned when the city fell (2 Kings 25:9)."}],"nm":{"EVT-01905":"Nebuzaradan burns the temple and Jerusalem","PER-01496":"Asaph"}},"OBJ-00448":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 80","d":"Asaph's prayer to the Shepherd of Israel to restore His vine brought out of Egypt (Psalm 80)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 80:1–19","v":"The Shepherd of Israel, who leads Joseph like a flock and dwells between the cherubim, is asked to stir up His strength before Ephraim, Benjamin and Manasseh and make His face shine; He brought a vine out of Egypt, cast out the nations and planted it, and it filled the land and sent its boughs to the Sea and its branches to the River; now its hedges are broken down and it is burned and cut down, and the psalm asks the LORD God of hosts to revive His people"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 80","v":"A Testimony of Asaph"},{"p":"feature","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 80:1; Psalms 80","v":"Set to 'The Lilies' (Hebrew Shoshannim); a Testimony (Hebrew Eduth)"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 80","e":"PER-01496"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 80","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"PER-01496":"Asaph"}},"OBJ-00449":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 81","d":"Asaph's call to keep the feast and to hear the LORD who brought Israel out of Egypt (Psalm 81)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 81:7; Psalms 81:1–16","v":"Israel is called to sing aloud to God and blow the trumpet at the New Moon and the full moon, a statute He set in Joseph when He went out over Egypt; He freed their shoulders from the burden, answered them from the thunder and tested them at the waters of Meribah (Strife, by the NKJV note); He forbids foreign gods, and laments that His people would not listen, for He would have subdued their enemies and fed them with the finest wheat and honey from the rock"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 81","v":"A Psalm of Asaph"},{"p":"feature","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 81:1; Psalms 81","v":"On an instrument of Gath (Hebrew Al Gittith)"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 81","e":"PER-01496"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 81","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"PER-01496":"Asaph"}},"OBJ-00450":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 82","d":"Asaph's psalm of God judging among the 'gods' (Psalm 82)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 82:1; Psalms 82:1–8; John 10:34–35","v":"God stands in the congregation of the mighty and judges among the 'gods' (judges, by the NKJV note), asking how long they will judge unjustly; they are to defend the poor and fatherless, but they walk in darkness, and though He called them gods and children of the Most High, words Jesus quotes, they will die like men; God is asked to arise and judge the earth"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 82","v":"A Psalm of Asaph"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 82","e":"PER-01496"}],"nm":{"PER-01496":"Asaph"}},"OBJ-00451":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 83","d":"Asaph's prayer against the confederacy of the nations conspiring to cut Israel off (Psalm 83)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 83:1–18","v":"God's enemies conspire to cut Israel off from being a nation: Edom, the Ishmaelites, Moab, the Hagrites, Gebal, Ammon, Amalek, Philistia with Tyre, and Assyria helping the children of Lot; Asaph asks God to deal with them as with Midian, as with Sisera and Jabin at the Brook Kishon, who perished at En Dor, and to make their nobles like Oreb and Zeeb and their princes like Zebah and Zalmunna, that they may know that He alone, whose name is the LORD, is the Most High over all the earth"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 83","v":"A Psalm of Asaph"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 83","v":"A Song"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 83","e":"PER-01496"}],"nm":{"PER-01496":"Asaph"}},"OBJ-00452":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 84","d":"The sons of Korah's psalm of longing for the courts of the LORD of hosts (Psalm 84)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 84:1–12","v":"The psalmist's soul longs for the courts of the LORD of hosts, where even the sparrow and swallow nest by His altars; blessed are those who dwell in His house and whose hearts are set on pilgrimage, who pass through the Valley of Baca and make it a spring, going from strength to strength until each appears before God in Zion; a day in His courts is better than a thousand, and the LORD God is a sun and shield to the upright"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 84","v":"A Psalm of the sons of Korah"},{"p":"feature","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 84:1; Psalms 84","v":"On an instrument of Gath (Hebrew Al Gittith)"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 84","e":"GRP-00086"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 84","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"GRP-00086":"Korahites"}},"OBJ-00453":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 85","d":"The sons of Korah's prayer that the LORD revive His people, having brought back Jacob's captivity (Psalm 85)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 85:1–13","v":"The LORD has been favorable to His land, brought back the captivity of Jacob and forgiven His people's sin; the psalmist asks Him to turn His anger away and revive them, and hears Him speak peace: mercy and truth have met together, righteousness and peace have kissed, and the land will yield its increase"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 85","v":"A Psalm of the sons of Korah"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 85","e":"GRP-00086"},{"p":"occasion","r":"Ezra 2:1; Psalms 85, 1","e":"EVT-02074","b":"inferred","c":"possible","w":"The psalm thanks God for bringing back the captivity of Jacob (Psalm 85:1), as the exiles came back from Babylon to Jerusalem and Judah (Ezra 2:1)."},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 85","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"EVT-02074":"The exiles return from Babylon with Zerubbabel","GRP-00086":"Korahites"}},"OBJ-00454":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 86","d":"David's prayer to the Lord, good and ready to forgive, for an undivided heart (Psalm 86)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 86:13; Psalms 86:1–17","v":"Poor and needy, David asks the Lord, good, ready to forgive and abundant in mercy, to hear him; none among the gods is like Him, and all nations He made will worship Him; David asks to be taught His way and given a united heart to fear His name, for He delivered his soul from the depths of Sheol, and asks for a sign for good against the proud"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 86","v":"A Prayer of David"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 86","e":"PER-00661"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00455":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 87","d":"The sons of Korah's song of Zion, the city of God, where the nations are counted as born (Psalm 87)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 87:4; Psalms 87:1–7","v":"The LORD founded His city on the holy mountains and loves the gates of Zion more than all the dwellings of Jacob; glorious things are spoken of the city of God; He will mention Rahab (Egypt, by the NKJV note) and Babylon, Philistia and Tyre with Ethiopia among those who know Him, and when He registers the peoples He will record that this one and that one were born in Zion"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 87","v":"A Psalm of the sons of Korah"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 87","v":"A Song"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 87","e":"GRP-00086"}],"nm":{"GRP-00086":"Korahites"}},"OBJ-00456":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 88","d":"The Contemplation of Heman the Ezrahite, crying from the edge of the grave (Psalm 88)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 88:1–18","v":"Crying day and night to the LORD, God of his salvation, Heman says his soul is full of troubles and his life near the grave; he is counted with those who go down to the pit, laid in darkness under God's wrath, and his acquaintances and loved ones are put far from him; he asks whether the dead will praise God, and why God hides His face, for he has been afflicted from his youth"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 88","v":"A Psalm of the sons of Korah"},{"p":"designation","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 88:1; Psalms 88","v":"A Contemplation of Heman the Ezrahite"},{"p":"feature","r":"Psalms 88","v":"Set to 'Mahalath Leannoth'"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 88","e":"GRP-00086"},{"p":"made by","r":"1 Kings 4:31; Psalms 88; 89","e":"PER-00933","b":"inferred","c":"probable","w":"The title calls him Heman the Ezrahite; Heman is named with Ethan the Ezrahite among the wisest of men (1 Kings 4:31), and Psalm 89 is by Ethan the Ezrahite."},{"p":"made by","r":"1 Chronicles 6:33–37; Psalms 88","e":"PER-01510","b":"inferred","c":"possible","s":"alternative","w":"The title also calls the psalm one of the sons of Korah, and Heman the singer descended from Korah (1 Chronicles 6:33–37)."},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 88","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"GRP-00086":"Korahites","PER-00933":"Heman","PER-01510":"Heman"}},"OBJ-00457":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 89","d":"The Contemplation of Ethan the Ezrahite on the LORD's covenant with David (Psalm 89)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 89:1–52","v":"Ethan sings of the LORD's mercies and faithfulness: He made a covenant with David His chosen, to establish his seed and throne forever; none in the heavens is like the LORD God of hosts, who rules the raging sea, broke Rahab in pieces and created north and south, so that Tabor and Hermon rejoice in His name; He anointed David with His holy oil, made him His firstborn, highest of the kings of the earth, and swore that if his sons forsook His law He would punish them but not break His covenant; yet now He has cast off His anointed, profaned his crown and ruined his strongholds, and Ethan asks how long; the psalm, and Book Three, end with a blessing of the LORD"},{"p":"designation","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 89:1; Psalms 89","v":"A Contemplation of Ethan the Ezrahite"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 89","e":"PER-00932"}],"nm":{"PER-00932":"Ethan"}},"OBJ-00458":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 90","d":"The prayer of Moses the man of God on God's eternity and man's frailty (Psalm 90)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 90:1; Psalms 90:1–17","v":"The Lord has been His people's dwelling place in all generations, God from everlasting before the mountains were born; a thousand years are to Him as yesterday, while men are swept away like grass that withers by evening; consumed by His wrath, they live seventy years, or eighty by strength, and Moses asks God to teach them to number their days, to satisfy them early with His mercy, and to establish the work of their hands"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 90","v":"A Prayer of Moses"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 90","e":"PER-00353"}],"nm":{"PER-00353":"Moses"}},"OBJ-00459":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 91","d":"The psalm of safety under the shadow of the Almighty (Psalm 91)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 91:1–16; Matthew 4:6","v":"One who dwells in the secret place of the Most High abides under the shadow of the Almighty, his refuge and fortress; He delivers him from the fowler's snare and the pestilence, so that he need not fear terror by night or arrow by day though thousands fall beside him, for God gives His angels charge to bear him up, words the tempter quoted to Jesus; because he loves God, God will deliver him and satisfy him with long life"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 91:1","v":"He who dwells in the secret place"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00460":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 92","d":"The song for the Sabbath day, giving thanks to the Most High (Psalm 92)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 92:1–15","v":"It is good to give thanks to the Most High, declaring His lovingkindness in the morning and His faithfulness at night with ten-stringed instrument, lute and harp; the wicked spring up like grass only to be destroyed, but the psalmist's horn is exalted and he is anointed with fresh oil; the righteous flourish like a palm and grow like a cedar in Lebanon, planted in the LORD's house and bearing fruit in old age"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 92","v":"A Song for the Sabbath day"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 92","v":"For the Sabbath day"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00461":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 93","d":"The psalm that the LORD reigns, mightier than the floods (Psalm 93)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 93:1–5","v":"The LORD reigns, clothed with majesty and strength; the world is established and His throne is from of old; the floods lift up their voice, but the LORD on high is mightier than the waves of the sea; His testimonies are sure, and holiness adorns His house forever"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 93:1","v":"The LORD reigns"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00462":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 94","d":"The prayer to God, to whom vengeance belongs, the Judge of the earth (Psalm 94)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 94:1–23","v":"The Judge of the earth is asked to repay the proud, who crush His people, kill the widow, the stranger and the fatherless, and say the LORD does not see; He who planted the ear and formed the eye hears and sees, and blessed is the man He instructs, for He will not cast off His people; the LORD has been the psalmist's defense and the rock of his refuge"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 94:1","v":"O God, to whom vengeance belongs"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00463":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 95","d":"The call to worship the LORD, and not to harden the heart as at Meribah (Psalm 95)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 95:1–11; Hebrews 3:7–11; 4:7","v":"All are called to sing to the Rock of their salvation, the great God and great King above all gods, who holds the depths and heights of the earth and made the sea and the dry land, and to kneel before the LORD their Maker, for they are the sheep of His pasture; today they must not harden their hearts as in the rebellion and the day of trial in the wilderness (Meribah and Massah, by the NKJV notes), when their fathers tested Him for forty years and He swore they would not enter His rest; Hebrews quotes the warning as said in David"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 95:1","v":"Oh come, let us sing"},{"p":"made by","r":"Hebrews 4:7","e":"PER-00661"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00464":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 96","d":"The new song to the LORD, who is coming to judge the earth (Psalm 96)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 96:1–13","v":"All the earth is called to sing the LORD a new song and declare His glory among the nations, for the gods of the peoples are idols but the LORD made the heavens; the families of the peoples are to give Him glory, bring an offering into His courts and worship Him in the beauty of holiness, saying among the nations that the LORD reigns; heaven, earth, sea, field and trees rejoice, for He is coming to judge the world with righteousness"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 96:1","v":"Oh, sing to the LORD"},{"p":"made by","r":"1 Chronicles 16:7, 23–33; Psalms 96:1–13","e":"PER-00661","b":"inferred","c":"probable","w":"Its words are, nearly all, in the psalm David first delivered to Asaph on the day the ark was set in its place (1 Chronicles 16:7, 23–33)."}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00465":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 97","d":"The psalm that the LORD reigns over the whole earth and Zion is glad (Psalm 97)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 97:1; Psalms 97:1–12","v":"The LORD reigns, and the earth and the many isles are to rejoice; clouds and darkness surround Him, righteousness and justice are the foundation of His throne, fire goes before Him and the mountains melt like wax before the Lord of the whole earth; those who serve images are put to shame, Zion hears and is glad, and light is sown for the righteous"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 97:1","v":"The LORD reigns; let the earth rejoice"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00466":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 98","d":"The psalm of a new song to the LORD, who has made known His salvation (Psalm 98)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 98:1–9","v":"All are called to sing the LORD a new song, for His right hand has won the victory and He has made known His salvation to the nations and remembered His mercy to Israel; the earth is to shout with harp, trumpets and horn before the LORD the King, the sea to roar and the rivers to clap their hands, for He is coming to judge the world with righteousness"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 98","v":"A Psalm"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00467":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 99","d":"The psalm of the holy LORD who reigns between the cherubim and answered Moses, Aaron and Samuel (Psalm 99)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 99:1–9","v":"The LORD reigns between the cherubim and is great in Zion, and His name is holy; He has done justice in Jacob; Moses and Aaron were among His priests and Samuel among those who called on His name, and He answered them and spoke to them in the cloudy pillar; He was God-Who-Forgives to them, though He punished their deeds; all are to worship at His holy hill"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 99:1","v":"The LORD reigns; let the peoples tremble"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00468":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 100","d":"The psalm of thanksgiving calling all lands to serve the LORD with gladness (Psalm 100)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 100:3; Psalms 100:1–5","v":"All lands are called to shout to the LORD, serve Him with gladness and know that He is God, who made them, His people and the sheep of His pasture; they are to enter His gates with thanksgiving and His courts with praise, for He is good and His mercy is everlasting"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 100","v":"A Psalm of Thanksgiving"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 100","v":"For thanksgiving"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00469":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 101","d":"David's vow to walk with a perfect heart and to cut off evildoers (Psalm 101)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 101:1–8","v":"David sings of mercy and justice and vows to walk in his house with a perfect heart, to set no wicked thing before his eyes, to destroy the slanderer and not endure the proud, to keep the faithful of the land near him and no liar in his presence, and early to cut off all evildoers from the city of the LORD"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 101","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 101","e":"PER-00661"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00470":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 102","d":"The prayer of one afflicted and overwhelmed, who asks the LORD to have mercy on Zion (Psalm 102)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 102:1–28; Hebrews 1:10–12","v":"The afflicted man's days vanish like smoke, he is like a lone sparrow on the housetop and eats ashes like bread under God's wrath; but the LORD endures forever and will arise and have mercy on Zion, for the set time has come and His servants love her stones; He will build up Zion and appear in His glory, and this will be written for a generation to come; He laid the earth's foundations, and while heaven and earth wear out like a garment, He remains the same, words Hebrews applies to the Son"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 102","v":"A Prayer of the afflicted"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 102","v":"For one overwhelmed, pouring out his complaint before the LORD"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00471":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 103","d":"David's psalm blessing the LORD for all His benefits and mercies (Psalm 103)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 103:1–22","v":"David bids his soul bless the LORD and forget none of His benefits: He forgives, heals, redeems and renews youth like the eagle's; He made His ways known to Moses; He is merciful and gracious, slow to anger, and removes transgressions as far as the east is from the west, pitying those who fear Him as a father pities his children, for man's days are like grass but His mercy is everlasting; His throne is in heaven, and His angels, hosts and works are to bless Him"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 103","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 103","e":"PER-00661"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00472":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 104","d":"The psalm blessing the LORD for His works in creation and His care for all He made (Psalm 104)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 104:18; NKJV notes, note on Psalm 104:26; Psalms 104:1–35","v":"The LORD is clothed with light and majesty; He stretches out the heavens, rides the clouds and makes His angels spirits; He set the earth on its foundations, covered it with the deep, then rebuked the waters and set them a boundary; He sends springs to the valleys, grass for cattle, and wine, oil and bread for man; He planted the cedars of Lebanon, gave the high hills to the wild goats and the cliffs to the rock badgers, and appointed the moon for seasons; the wide sea holds countless creatures, the ships and Leviathan; all wait on Him for food, and when He sends forth His Spirit they are created and the earth renewed"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 104:1","v":"Bless the LORD, O my soul"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00473":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 105","d":"The psalm of the LORD's faithfulness to His covenant from Abraham to the land of Canaan (Psalm 105)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 105:18; Psalms 105:1–45","v":"The seed of Abraham are called to give thanks and remember the covenant the LORD made with Abraham, swore to Isaac and confirmed to Jacob, to give them Canaan; when they were few and strangers He let no one wrong them and rebuked kings for them; He called a famine and sent Joseph ahead, sold as a slave and laid in irons until the king released him and made him lord of his house; Israel came into the land of Ham, and Moses and Aaron worked His signs there; He brought His people out with silver and gold, gave them a cloud for covering and fire for light, quail, bread from heaven and water from the rock, and gave them the lands of the nations, that they might keep His laws"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 105:1","v":"Oh, give thanks to the LORD"},{"p":"made by","r":"1 Chronicles 16:7–22; Psalms 105:1–15","e":"PER-00661","b":"inferred","c":"possible","w":"Its first fifteen verses are in the psalm David first delivered to Asaph on the day the ark was set in its place (1 Chronicles 16:7–22)."}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00474":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 106","d":"The psalm confessing Israel's sins from the Red Sea to Canaan and the LORD's many deliverances (Psalm 106)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 106:32; Psalms 106:1–48","v":"The psalmist gives thanks to the LORD, whose mercy endures forever, and confesses that Israel sinned with their fathers: they rebelled at the Red Sea, yet He saved them; they lusted in the wilderness and He sent leanness; they envied Moses and Aaron, made a calf in Horeb, despised the pleasant land and joined Baal of Peor, and angered Him at the waters of strife (Meribah, by the NKJV note); in the land they mingled with the nations, served their idols and sacrificed their children to demons, so He gave them into the hands of their enemies, yet many times delivered them and made their captors pity them; he prays to be gathered from among the nations, and Book Four closes with a blessing of the LORD God of Israel"},{"p":"designation","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 106:1; Psalms 106:1","v":"Praise the LORD"},{"p":"made by","r":"1 Chronicles 16:7, 34–36; Psalms 106:1, 47–48","e":"PER-00661","b":"inferred","c":"possible","w":"Its first and last verses are in the psalm David first delivered to Asaph on the day the ark was set in its place (1 Chronicles 16:7, 34–36)."}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00475":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 107","d":"The thanksgiving of the redeemed whom the LORD gathered from every land (Psalm 107)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 107:34; Psalms 107:1–43","v":"The redeemed, gathered from east, west, north and south, are bidden to give thanks to the LORD for His goodness: wanderers in the desolate wilderness He led to a city to dwell in; prisoners in darkness for rebelling against the Most High He freed, breaking gates of bronze; fools near death He healed by sending His word; and sailors whose storm He calmed He guided to their haven; He turns rivers into wilderness and fruitful land into a salty waste for the wickedness of its people, and wilderness into pools where the hungry build a city"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 107:1","v":"Oh, give thanks to the LORD"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00476":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 108","d":"David's song of a steadfast heart and of God's victory over Edom (Psalm 108)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 57:7–11; 60:5–12; 108:1–13","v":"David's heart is steadfast to sing and awaken the dawn and praise the LORD among the nations, for His mercy is above the heavens; God has spoken that He will divide Shechem and measure out the Valley of Succoth, that Gilead, Manasseh, Ephraim and Judah are His, Moab His washpot, Edom under His shoe and Philistia His triumph; through God His people will do valiantly; the psalm joins the close of Psalm 57 to the close of Psalm 60"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 108","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 108","v":"A Song"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 108","e":"PER-00661"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00477":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 109","d":"David's plea that God judge his false accusers (Psalm 109)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 109:6; Psalms 109:1–31; Acts 1:20","v":"David asks the God of his praise not to keep silent, for lying accusers repay his love with hatred; he prays that an accuser (Hebrew satan, by the NKJV note) stand at the wicked man's right hand, that his days be few and another take his office, words Acts applies to Judas, and that his name be blotted out; poor, needy and weak from fasting, David asks the LORD to save him, for He stands at the right hand of the poor"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 109","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 109; Acts 1:16, 20","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 109","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00478":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 110","d":"David's psalm of the LORD's word to his Lord, a priest forever after the order of Melchizedek (Psalm 110)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 110:1–7; Matthew 22:43–45; Acts 2:34–35; Hebrews 1:13; 5:6; 7:17","v":"The LORD said to David's Lord, sit at My right hand till I make Your enemies Your footstool, words Jesus, Acts and Hebrews apply to the Christ; the LORD will send the rod of His strength out of Zion, His people will offer themselves willingly in the day of His power, and the LORD has sworn that He is a priest forever according to the order of Melchizedek; the Lord at His right hand will break kings in the day of His wrath and judge the nations"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 110","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 110; Matthew 22:43–45; Luke 20:42; Acts 2:34","e":"PER-00661"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00479":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 111","d":"The praise of the LORD's great works, whose fear is the beginning of wisdom (Psalm 111)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 111:1–10","v":"The psalmist praises the LORD with his whole heart in the congregation: His works are great and glorious, He is gracious and full of compassion, has given food to those who fear Him, keeps His covenant, gave His people the heritage of the nations and sent them redemption; holy and awesome is His name, and the fear of the LORD is the beginning of wisdom"},{"p":"designation","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 111:1; Psalms 111:1","v":"Praise the LORD"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00480":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 112","d":"The psalm of the blessed man who fears the LORD (Psalm 112)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 112:1–10; 2 Corinthians 9:9","v":"Blessed is the man who fears the LORD and delights in His commandments: his descendants will be mighty and his house rich, light rises for him in darkness, he lends graciously and gives to the poor, words Paul quotes, his heart is steadfast and unafraid of evil tidings, and his righteousness endures forever, while the desire of the wicked perishes"},{"p":"designation","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 112:1; Psalms 112:1","v":"Praise the LORD"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00481":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 113","d":"The psalm of the LORD high above the nations, who raises the poor from the dust (Psalm 113)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 113:1–9","v":"The servants of the LORD are to praise His name from the rising of the sun to its setting; He is high above all nations and dwells on high, yet humbles Himself to look on heaven and earth, raises the poor from the dust to sit with princes, and gives the barren woman a home as a joyful mother of children"},{"p":"designation","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 113:1; Psalms 113:1","v":"Praise the LORD"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00482":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 114","d":"The psalm of Israel's going out of Egypt, when the sea fled and the Jordan turned back (Psalm 114)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 114:1; Psalms 114:1–8","v":"When Israel went out of Egypt, from a people of strange language, Judah became God's sanctuary and Israel His dominion; the sea saw it and fled, the Jordan turned back, the mountains skipped like rams and the hills like lambs; the earth is to tremble before the God of Jacob, who turned the rock into a pool and the flint into a fountain"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 114:1","v":"When Israel went out of Egypt"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00483":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 115","d":"The psalm giving glory not to us but to the LORD's name, and mocking idols (Psalm 115)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 115:1–18","v":"Glory belongs not to His people but to the LORD's name; their God is in heaven and does whatever He pleases, while the idols of the nations are silver and gold that cannot speak, see, hear or walk, and their makers are like them; Israel, the house of Aaron and all who fear the LORD are to trust Him as their help and shield, for He will bless them; the heavens are His, but He has given the earth to the children of men"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 115:1","v":"Not unto us, O LORD"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00484":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 116","d":"The thanksgiving of one the LORD delivered from death, paying his vows in Jerusalem (Psalm 116)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 116:1–19; 2 Corinthians 4:13","v":"The psalmist loves the LORD, who heard him when the pains of death and Sheol took hold of him and delivered his soul from death, his eyes from tears and his feet from falling; he believed and therefore spoke, words Paul quotes; he will take up the cup of salvation and pay his vows before all the people in the courts of the LORD's house in Jerusalem, for the death of His saints is precious in His sight"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 116:1","v":"I love the LORD"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00485":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 117","d":"The shortest psalm, calling all nations to praise the LORD (Psalm 117)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 117:1–2; Romans 15:11","v":"All Gentiles and peoples are called to praise the LORD, words Paul quotes, for His merciful kindness toward His people is great and His truth endures forever"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 117:1","v":"Praise the LORD, all you Gentiles"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00486":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 118","d":"The psalm of the LORD's enduring mercy and the stone the builders rejected (Psalm 118)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 118:1–29; Matthew 21:9, 42; Acts 4:11","v":"Israel, the house of Aaron and all who fear the LORD are to say that His mercy endures forever; the psalmist called in distress and the LORD answered, so he will not fear man, for it is better to trust the LORD than princes; all nations surrounded him like bees, but in the LORD's name he cut them off; he will not die but live; the gates of righteousness open to him, the stone the builders rejected has become the chief cornerstone, this is the day the LORD has made, and blessed is he who comes in the name of the LORD, words the Gospels and Acts apply to Jesus"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 118:1","v":"Oh, give thanks to the LORD"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00487":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 119","d":"The longest psalm, in twenty-two alphabetic stanzas on the word of God (Psalm 119)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 119:89; Psalms 119:1–176","v":"The psalmist blesses those who walk in the LORD's law and keep His testimonies; a young man keeps his way pure by heeding His word, which the psalmist hides in his heart so as not to sin; he asks to have his eyes opened to wonders in the law, sings the statutes as a stranger on the earth, rises at midnight to give thanks, and finds it good that he was afflicted; the LORD's word is settled forever in heaven; he loves the law and meditates on it all day, finds it sweeter than honey, a lamp to his feet and a light to his path, weeps because men do not keep it, praises God seven times a day, and ends asking God to seek him, for he has strayed like a lost sheep yet does not forget His commandments"},{"p":"designation","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 119:1; Psalms 119:1","v":"Blessed are the undefiled in the way"},{"p":"feature","r":"Psalms 119:1–176","v":"Twenty-two stanzas of eight verses, each headed in order by a letter of the Hebrew alphabet, from Aleph to Tau"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00488":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 120","d":"The Song of Ascents of one who dwells too long among those who hate peace, in Meshech and Kedar (Psalm 120)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 120:1–7","v":"In distress the psalmist cries to the LORD to deliver him from lying lips and a deceitful tongue, which will be repaid with a warrior's arrows and coals of broom; woe to him that he dwells in Meshech among the tents of Kedar, with those who hate peace, for when he speaks for peace they are for war"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 120","v":"A Song of Ascents"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00489":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 121","d":"The Song of Ascents of help from the LORD, Israel's keeper who never sleeps (Psalm 121)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 121:1–8","v":"The psalmist lifts his eyes to the hills and declares that his help comes from the LORD, maker of heaven and earth; He who keeps Israel neither slumbers nor sleeps, is His people's shade, and will keep them from all evil, in their going out and coming in, forever"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 121","v":"A Song of Ascents"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00490":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 122","d":"David's Song of Ascents of the joy of going up to the house of the LORD in Jerusalem (Psalm 122)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 122:4; Psalms 122:1–9","v":"David was glad when told they would go to the house of the LORD; their feet stand within the gates of Jerusalem, built as a city compact together, where the tribes of the LORD go up to give thanks to His name and the thrones of David's house are set for judgment; all are to pray for her peace, for peace within her walls and prosperity in her palaces"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 122","v":"A Song of Ascents"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 122","e":"PER-00661"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00491":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 123","d":"The Song of Ascents of eyes lifted to the LORD for mercy (Psalm 123)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 123:1–4","v":"The people lift their eyes to the LORD who dwells in the heavens, as servants look to their master's hand, until He has mercy, for they are filled with the scorn of those at ease and the contempt of the proud"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 123","v":"A Song of Ascents"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00492":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 124","d":"David's Song of Ascents: had the LORD not been on Israel's side (Psalm 124)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 124:7; Psalms 124:1–8","v":"Israel is to say that had the LORD not been on their side when men rose up against them, they would have been swallowed alive and swept away by the waters; blessed be the LORD, for they escaped like a bird from the fowlers' snare, and their help is in the name of the LORD, maker of heaven and earth"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 124","v":"A Song of Ascents"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 124","e":"PER-00661"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00493":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 125","d":"The Song of Ascents of those who trust in the LORD, unmoved like Mount Zion (Psalm 125)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 125:1–5","v":"Those who trust in the LORD are like Mount Zion, which cannot be moved; as the mountains surround Jerusalem, so the LORD surrounds His people forever; the scepter of wickedness will not rest on the land of the righteous, and the LORD will do good to the upright but lead away those who turn to crooked ways; peace be on Israel"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 125","v":"A Song of Ascents"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00494":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 126","d":"The Song of Ascents of the captivity of Zion brought back (Psalm 126)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 126:1; Psalms 126:1–6","v":"When the LORD brought back the captivity of Zion they were like dreamers, their mouths filled with laughter, and the nations said the LORD had done great things for them; they ask Him to bring back their captivity like streams in the South, for those who sow in tears will reap in joy and come again bringing their sheaves"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 126","v":"A Song of Ascents"},{"p":"occasion","r":"Ezra 2:1; Psalms 126:1","e":"EVT-02074","b":"inferred","c":"possible","w":"The psalm remembers when the LORD brought back the captivity of Zion (Psalm 126:1), as the exiles came back from Babylon to Jerusalem and Judah (Ezra 2:1)."}],"nm":{"EVT-02074":"The exiles return from Babylon with Zerubbabel"}},"OBJ-00495":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 127","d":"Solomon's Song of Ascents: unless the LORD builds the house (Psalm 127)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 127:1–5","v":"Unless the LORD builds the house its builders labor in vain, and unless He guards the city the watchman wakes in vain; it is vain to rise early and toil late, for He gives His beloved sleep; children are a heritage from the LORD, like arrows in a warrior's hand, and happy is the man whose quiver is full of them"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 127","v":"A Song of Ascents"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 127","e":"PER-00765"}],"nm":{"PER-00765":"Solomon"}},"OBJ-00496":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 128","d":"The Song of Ascents of the blessed home of one who fears the LORD (Psalm 128)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 128:1–6","v":"Blessed is everyone who fears the LORD and walks in His ways: he will eat the labor of his hands, his wife will be like a fruitful vine in his house and his children like olive plants around his table; may the LORD bless him out of Zion, may he see the good of Jerusalem all his days and his children's children"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 128","v":"A Song of Ascents"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00497":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 129","d":"The Song of Ascents of Israel afflicted from her youth but not overcome (Psalm 129)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 129:1–8","v":"Israel is to say that many a time she has been afflicted from her youth, the plowers plowing long furrows on her back, yet they have not prevailed, for the righteous LORD has cut the cords of the wicked; those who hate Zion are to wither like grass on the housetops, unblessed by passersby"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 129","v":"A Song of Ascents"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00498":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 130","d":"The Song of Ascents crying to the LORD out of the depths (Psalm 130)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 130:1–8","v":"Out of the depths the psalmist cries to the LORD: if He marked iniquities none could stand, but there is forgiveness with Him; his soul waits for the LORD more than watchmen for the morning, and Israel is to hope in Him, for with Him is abundant redemption"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 130","v":"A Song of Ascents"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00499":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 131","d":"David's Song of Ascents of a soul calmed like a weaned child (Psalm 131)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 131:1–3","v":"David's heart is not proud nor does he busy himself with things too great for him; he has calmed and quieted his soul like a weaned child with its mother, and bids Israel hope in the LORD forever"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 131","v":"A Song of Ascents"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 131","e":"PER-00661"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00500":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 132","d":"The Song of Ascents of David's vow to find a dwelling for the LORD, and the LORD's choice of Zion (Psalm 132)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 132:6; NKJV notes, note on Psalm 132:17; Psalms 132:1–18","v":"The LORD is asked to remember David's afflictions and his vow to the Mighty One of Jacob not to sleep until he found a dwelling for the LORD; they heard of it in Ephrathah and found it in the fields of the woods (Jaar, by the NKJV note); the LORD is to arise to His resting place with the ark of His strength and not turn away from His Anointed, for He swore to David that his offspring would sit on his throne if they kept His covenant, and He has chosen Zion as His resting place forever, where He will make the horn of David grow and prepare a lamp for His Anointed"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 132","v":"A Song of Ascents"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00501":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 133","d":"David's Song of Ascents of brethren dwelling together in unity (Psalm 133)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 133:1–3","v":"It is good and pleasant for brethren to dwell together in unity: it is like the precious oil on the head running down Aaron's beard to the edge of his garments, and like the dew of Hermon descending on the mountains of Zion, where the LORD commanded the blessing of life forevermore"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 133","v":"A Song of Ascents"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 133","e":"PER-00661"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00502":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 134","d":"The last Song of Ascents, calling the LORD's servants in His house by night to bless Him (Psalm 134)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 134:1–3","v":"All the servants of the LORD who stand by night in the house of the LORD are called to lift their hands in the sanctuary and bless Him, and the LORD who made heaven and earth is asked to bless them from Zion"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 134","v":"A Song of Ascents"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00503":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 135","d":"The praise of the LORD who chose Israel, struck Egypt and gave Israel the land of Sihon and Og (Psalm 135)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 135:4; Psalms 135:1–21","v":"The servants who stand in the courts of the LORD's house are to praise Him, for He chose Jacob as His special treasure and is above all gods, doing whatever He pleases in heaven, earth and sea; He struck the firstborn of Egypt, man and beast, sent signs on Pharaoh and his servants, slew Sihon king of the Amorites, Og king of Bashan and all the kingdoms of Canaan, and gave their land to Israel as a heritage; the idols of the nations cannot speak or see; the houses of Israel, Aaron and Levi are to bless the LORD, who dwells in Jerusalem"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 135:1","v":"Praise the LORD"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00504":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 136","d":"The thanksgiving whose every verse answers that His mercy endures forever (Psalm 136)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 136:1–26","v":"Thanks are given to the God of gods and Lord of lords, who alone does great wonders: who made the heavens by wisdom, laid the earth above the waters and made the great lights, the sun by day and the moon and stars by night; who struck Egypt's firstborn and brought Israel out with a strong hand, divided the Red Sea, overthrew Pharaoh and his army in it and led His people through the wilderness; who slew Sihon king of the Amorites and Og king of Bashan and gave their land to Israel; who remembered them in their low estate and gives food to all flesh; thanks to the God of heaven"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 136:1","v":"Oh, give thanks to the LORD"},{"p":"feature","r":"Psalms 136:1–26","v":"Every verse closes with the refrain that His mercy endures forever"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00505":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 137","d":"The lament of the captives by the rivers of Babylon, who remembered Zion (Psalm 137)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 137:7; Psalms 137:1–9","v":"By the rivers of Babylon the captives sat and wept when they remembered Zion and hung their harps on the willows, for their captors asked them for songs of Zion and they could not sing the LORD's song in a foreign land; the psalmist swears never to forget Jerusalem, asks the LORD to remember against the sons of Edom the day of Jerusalem, when they cried to raze it to its foundation, and pronounces a blessing on whoever repays the daughter of Babylon"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 137:1","v":"By the rivers of Babylon"},{"p":"occasion","r":"2 Kings 25:11; Psalms 137:1–3, 7","e":"EVT-01906","b":"inferred","c":"probable","w":"The psalm is sung by captives sitting by the rivers of Babylon who remember Zion and the day of Jerusalem (Psalm 137:1–7); Nebuzaradan carried the people of Jerusalem away to the king of Babylon (2 Kings 25:11)."}],"nm":{"EVT-01906":"Nebuzaradan carries the people of Jerusalem captive"}},"OBJ-00506":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 138","d":"David's thanks with his whole heart to the LORD, who regards the lowly (Psalm 138)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 138:1–8","v":"David praises the LORD with his whole heart before the gods and worships toward His holy temple, for He answered him when he cried and has magnified His word above all His name; all the kings of the earth will praise Him; the LORD on high regards the lowly but knows the proud from afar, and He will revive David in trouble and perfect what concerns him"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 138","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 138","e":"PER-00661"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00507":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 139","d":"David's psalm of the LORD who has searched and known him and formed him in the womb (Psalm 139)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 139:8; Psalms 139:1–24","v":"The LORD has searched and known David, his sitting and rising, his thoughts and every word; he cannot flee from His Spirit, for in heaven or Sheol, at the far end of the sea or in darkness, God is there; God formed his inward parts and wove him in his mother's womb, he is fearfully and wonderfully made, and all his days were written in God's book before one of them came; he asks God to slay the wicked, and to search him and lead him in the everlasting way"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 139","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 139","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 139","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00508":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 140","d":"David's prayer to be kept from violent men with serpents' tongues (Psalm 140)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 140:1–13","v":"David asks the LORD to keep him from violent men who plan evil, sharpen their tongues like a serpent and set snares for him; God the Lord, the strength of his salvation, covered his head in the day of battle; he asks that burning coals fall on his enemies, for the LORD will maintain the cause of the afflicted and the upright will dwell in His presence"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 140","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 140","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"purpose","r":"Psalms 140","v":"Given to the Chief Musician"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00509":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 141","d":"David's prayer that his prayer rise like incense and his lips be guarded (Psalm 141)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 141:1–10","v":"David asks that his prayer be set before the LORD as incense and the lifting of his hands as the evening sacrifice, that a guard be set over his mouth and his heart not turn to evil; he welcomes the rebuke of the righteous, keeps his eyes on God the Lord, and asks to be kept from the snares of the wicked, who will fall into their own nets"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 141","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 141","e":"PER-00661"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00510":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 142","d":"David's Contemplation, a prayer when he was in the cave (Psalm 142)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 142:1–7","v":"David pours out his complaint to the LORD: when his spirit was overwhelmed God knew his path, though snares were set for him and no one cared for his soul; the LORD is his refuge and his portion in the land of the living, and he asks to be delivered from persecutors stronger than he and brought out of prison to praise His name"},{"p":"designation","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 142:1; Psalms 142","v":"A Contemplation of David"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 142","v":"A Prayer when he was in the cave"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 142","e":"PER-00661"},{"p":"occasion","r":"1 Samuel 22:1; 24:3; Psalms 142","e":"EVT-01119","b":"inferred","c":"possible","w":"The title sets the prayer when David was in the cave: he escaped to the cave of Adullam (1 Samuel 22:1), and later hid in a cave in the wilderness of En Gedi when Saul came in (1 Samuel 24:3)."},{"p":"occasion","r":"1 Samuel 22:1; 24:3; Psalms 142","e":"EVT-01138","b":"inferred","c":"possible","w":"The title sets the prayer when David was in the cave: he escaped to the cave of Adullam (1 Samuel 22:1), and later hid in a cave in the wilderness of En Gedi when Saul came in (1 Samuel 24:3)."}],"nm":{"EVT-01119":"David gathers four hundred men at the cave of Adullam","EVT-01138":"David spares Saul in the cave","PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00511":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 143","d":"David's plea not to be judged, and to be taught to do God's will (Psalm 143)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 143:1–12","v":"David asks the LORD to answer in His faithfulness and not enter into judgment with His servant, for no one living is righteous before Him; crushed by the enemy and dwelling in darkness, he remembers the days of old and thirsts for God like a dry land; he asks to hear His lovingkindness in the morning, to be taught to do His will, and to be led by His good Spirit in the land of uprightness"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 143","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 143","e":"PER-00661"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00512":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 144","d":"David's song of the LORD his Rock, who trains his hands for war (Psalm 144)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 144:1–15","v":"Blessed be the LORD, David's Rock, who trains his hands for war and is his fortress, high tower, deliverer and shield; man is like a breath, yet the LORD is asked to bow the heavens, come down and rescue David from foreigners whose words are lies; David will sing a new song on a harp of ten strings to the One who gives salvation to kings and delivers David His servant from the deadly sword; happy is the people whose sons and daughters flourish, whose barns and flocks are full, and whose God is the LORD"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 144","v":"A Psalm of David"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 144","e":"PER-00661"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00513":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 145","d":"David's Praise of God the King, whose kingdom is everlasting (Psalm 145)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 145:13; Psalms 145:1–21","v":"David extols God the King and will bless His name every day; His greatness is beyond searching, and each generation will declare His mighty acts to the next; the LORD is gracious, full of compassion, slow to anger and great in mercy, good to all; His kingdom is everlasting; He upholds all who fall, gives all their food in due season, is near to all who call on Him in truth, and preserves all who love Him but destroys the wicked"},{"p":"designation","r":"Psalms 145","v":"A Praise of David"},{"p":"made by","r":"Psalms 145","e":"PER-00661"}],"nm":{"PER-00661":"David"}},"OBJ-00514":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 146","d":"The Hallelujah psalm of trust in the God of Jacob rather than in princes (Psalm 146)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 146:1–10","v":"The psalmist will praise the LORD all his life; no one is to trust in princes, whose plans perish when their breath departs, but happy is he whose help is the God of Jacob, maker of heaven, earth and sea, who keeps truth, does justice for the oppressed, feeds the hungry, frees prisoners, opens the eyes of the blind and watches over strangers, the fatherless and the widow; the LORD, Zion's God, will reign forever"},{"p":"designation","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 146:1; Psalms 146:1","v":"Praise the LORD"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00515":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 147","d":"The Hallelujah psalm of the LORD who builds up Jerusalem and counts the stars (Psalm 147)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 147:20; Psalms 147:1–20","v":"It is good to praise God, for the LORD builds up Jerusalem, gathers the outcasts of Israel and heals the brokenhearted; He counts the stars and calls them by name, sends rain and grass and feeds the beasts and the young ravens, delighting not in the strength of horse or man but in those who fear Him; Jerusalem and Zion are to praise Him, for He has strengthened the bars of their gates, blessed their children and given peace in their borders; He sends snow, frost and hail and melts them by His word, and has declared His statutes to Jacob as to no other nation"},{"p":"designation","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 147:1; Psalms 147:1","v":"Praise the LORD"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00516":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 148","d":"The Hallelujah psalm calling all creation in heaven and earth to praise the LORD (Psalm 148)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 148:14; Psalms 148:1–14","v":"All in the heavens, His angels and hosts, sun, moon and stars and the waters above the heavens are to praise the LORD, for He commanded and they were created; and from the earth the sea creatures and the depths, fire, hail, snow and wind, mountains, trees and cedars, beasts and birds, kings, peoples, young and old are to praise His name, which alone is exalted; He has exalted the horn of His people Israel, a people near to Him"},{"p":"designation","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 148:1; Psalms 148:1","v":"Praise the LORD"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00517":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 149","d":"The Hallelujah psalm of Israel rejoicing in their Maker and King (Psalm 149)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"Psalms 149:1–9","v":"A new song is to be sung in the assembly of saints: Israel is to rejoice in their Maker and the children of Zion in their King, praising Him with dance, timbrel and harp, for He takes pleasure in His people; with God's high praises in their mouths and a two-edged sword in their hands the saints are to execute the written judgment on the nations and bind their kings with chains"},{"p":"designation","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 149:1; Psalms 149:1","v":"Praise the LORD"}],"nm":{}},"OBJ-00518":{"k":"object","n":"Psalm 150","d":"The last psalm: let everything that has breath praise the LORD (Psalm 150)","f":[{"p":"contents","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 150:1; Psalms 150:1–6","v":"God is to be praised in His sanctuary and in His mighty firmament, for His mighty acts and excellent greatness, with every instrument, and everything that has breath is to praise the LORD; the psalm closes the Book of Psalms"},{"p":"designation","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 150:1; Psalms 150:1","v":"Praise the LORD"},{"p":"feature","r":"NKJV notes, note on Psalm 150:3; Psalms 150:3–5","v":"It calls for praise with trumpet, lute, harp, timbrel, dance, stringed instruments, flutes and loud and clashing cymbals"}],"nm":{}}});
